<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burj Khalifa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2010</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Burj <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a> is a skyscraper in Dubai, at 828 metres the tallest building in the world since its opening on 4 January 2010. Developed by Emaar and designed by Adrian Smith of Skidmore, Owings &amp; Merrill, it was renamed at its opening from Burj Dubai in honour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa-bin-zayed-al-nahyan">Khalifa bin Zayed Al Nahyan</a>, president of the UAE, after Abu Dhabi's financial support for Dubai during the debt crisis of 2009.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burj-khalifa.jpg" alt="Burj Khalifa" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: imran shahabuddin · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burj_Khalifa_(worlds_tallest_building)_and_the_Dubai_skyline_(25781049892).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
